Bundled third-party code, included in shader-roulette.html and vendor/:

- mp4-muxer 5.2.2 by Vanilagy, MIT License (https://github.com/Vanilagy/mp4-muxer).
- AAC encoder (vendor/aac-wasm.js), kept in its own <script> block:
  FFmpeg libavcodec AAC encoder compiled to WebAssembly, LGPL-2.1-or-later
  (https://ffmpeg.org), with the bridge from @mediabunny/aac-encoder 1.61.3 by
  Vanilagy, MPL-2.0 (https://github.com/Vanilagy/mediabunny). These keep their
  own licenses, not MIT. License texts are in vendor/licenses/.
- SuperTool effect shaders (vendor/supertool-effects.json, from
  github.com/hughesdo/SuperTool public/shaders/effects). Each shader keeps the
  header, credits and licence its file came with.

Shaders and transitions loaded from the Shader-Selector library at runtime
belong to their original authors; each one's shader.json credits the creator
and links back to the original.
